WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — eco-avalanche (45s) Narrator Cecily

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.527
First, across life and computing, intelligence climbs a nine-step ladder through one repeating signal ratchet.

2
00:00:07.967 --> 00:00:11.069
Second, today's AI stalls at step five,

3
00:00:11.069 --> 00:00:16.001
tool use, because routine jobs wake giant models from scratch.

4
00:00:16.441 --> 00:00:21.134
Third, compiling verified answers into low-energy lookup reflexes

5
00:00:21.134 --> 00:00:24.672
crosses that wall and unlocks the top four steps.

6
00:00:25.112 --> 00:00:31.339
Imagine if your brain had to calculate every heartbeat and footstep consciously from scratch.

7
00:00:31.339 --> 00:00:38.302
Biology survived by practicing new motions once, then pushing proven patterns into fast spinal reflexes.

8
00:00:38.742 --> 00:00:43.441
Modern AI burns megawatts recalculating solved tasks at step five;

9
00:00:43.441 --> 00:00:50.491
compiling certified answers downward unlocks quiet wakeups, tiny lookup circuits, and global scale.
